.TH BINGUX-MEDIA 1 "2026-11-09" "Bingux 0.1.0" "Bingux"
.SH NAME
bingux-media \- music and video player for the Bingux desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bingux-media
.RI [ FILE | FOLDER | URI ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bingux-media
opens the Media window: the songs, albums, artists and videos in the Music and
Videos folders, a queue and a player.
With no argument it opens the library, or raises the window when it is already
open.
.PP
Only one Media window runs.
A second launch hands its files to the running window, which plays them.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I FILE
A song or video to play.
.TP
.I FOLDER
A folder; the songs and videos in it play in name order.
.TP
.I URI
A
.B file://
URI, or a
.B bingux-media://
address such as
.BR bingux-media://videos .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
End of options, for a name that starts with
.BR \- .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BINGUX_MEDIA_RENDER
.B sw
draws video with mpv's software renderer;
.B gl
uses the GPU renderer even on a software OpenGL driver.
.TP
.B BINGUX_MEDIA_AO
mpv's audio output, such as
.B pipewire
or
.BR null .
.TP
.B BINGUX_MEDIA_MPV_LOG
mpv's log level on standard error, such as
.BR v .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/bingux-media/settings.json
Settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/bingux-media/lastfm.json
The Last.fm key, secret and session, readable by the owner only.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/bingux-media/library.db
The library index, resume points and play counts.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/thumbnails/large/
Video thumbnails, shared with other programs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bingux-files (1),
.BR mpv (1)
